  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Bluff/IDI. Shedding + deduction. All cards dealt. Players claim current rank face-down. Challenge = loser takes pile. First to empty hand wins.',
    Player: "The current rank is 7s. You have no 7s! Play 2 cards face-down and claim 'Two Sevens'. Risky—but if your opponents aren't counting, they won't know there have already been three 7s played. If no one challenges, you shed 2 cards for free!",
    objective: 'Be the first player to empty your hand of all cards.',
    gameplay: "1. **Establish Rank**: A target rank (e.g., Queens) is chosen for the round. 2. **Turn**: Each player in turn must play 1 to 4 cards face-down, claiming they are the target rank. 3. **Challenge**: Any player can shout 'Bluff!' or 'I Doubt It!' after a play. 4. **Reveal**: If challenged, the played cards are revealed. 5. **Penalty**: If the player lied, they take the entire table pile. If they were truthful, the challenger takes the pile. 6. **Rank Change**: The rank changes to the next in sequence (A-2-3...) after a successful challenge or when a new round starts.",
    keyRules: [
      'You must play at least one card every turn.',
      "Any player can challenge any other player's claim.",
      'Successful challenges reset the central pile.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 to 6 players playing individually.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card French pack (No Jokers).',
      equipment: 'Standard pack.',
      dealing: 'Deal the entire deck as evenly as possible clockwise. Players keep their hands private but their card count visible.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Establish Rank**: A target rank (e.g., Queens) is chosen for the round. 2. **Turn**: Each player in turn must play 1 to 4 cards face-down, claiming they are the target rank. 3. **Challenge**: Any player can shout 'Bluff!' or 'I Doubt It!' after a play. 4. **Reveal**: If challenged, the played cards are revealed. 5. **Penalty**: If the player lied, they take the entire table pile. If they were truthful, the challenger takes the pile. 6. **Rank Change**: The rank changes to the next in sequence (A-2-3...) after a successful challenge or when a new round starts.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Bluff is a social shedding game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante system.',
      deal: 'The entire deck distribution at the start of the game is handled automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'There is no shared community market in Bluff; cards move from hands to a face-down central pile.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they only shed cards via claims.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at the start; no cards remain in stock to be purchased during play.',
      fold: "Participation is mandatory for every turn until a player's hand is completely exhausted to win.",
      check: 'The game uses a claiming structure rather than a vying structure where checking would be an option.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Bluff; competition is based on deception and shedding.',
      bet: 'Success is determined by emptying the hand rather than through the wagering of chips or currency.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in this game, so the value of the round cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Mandatory turn action when playing cards face-down.',
      reveal_hand: "Hands stay private; only specific cards are revealed during a successful 'Bluff' challenge.",
      award_pot: 'There is no central pot of points or chips to be awarded to a winner in this shedding game.',
      play_card: 'Mandatory each turn until the hand is empty.',
      draw: 'Cards are only acquired by failing or wrongly making a challenge rather than a standard draw action.',
      discard: 'Cards are played face-down to the table rather than being discarded to a waste pile.',
      pass: 'Any player can pass on their turn; the lead rank must be followed when other players play.',
      bid: 'Bluff does not utilize a bidding system to determine the dealer or game objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a shedding game based on deception rather than creating melds on the table.',
